{
  "hypothesis": "The kernel stores a scalar mean into a 1D output tensor using a vectorized store operation. This causes the scalar value to be broadcast and written to all elements of the output row, rather than just the first element. Consequently, only the first element of the output tensor contains the correct mean, while all subsequent elements are incorrectly populated with the same value.",
  "reference_expression": "mean_last(x0, False)",
  "candidate_expression": "mean_last(x0, False)",
  "repair_plan": "Modify the kernel to store the scalar mean only to the first element of the output row. Change the store operation to use a mask that is true only for index 0, or store to a pointer offset by 0 with a scalar store operation. Ensure the output tensor is allocated with the correct shape (rows,) and that the kernel writes exactly one value per row."
}
